# Task 145-027: Memory V2 Prod-Readiness Validation + 1000-Entry Stress

## Plan

### Test 1: Prod-Readiness E2E (tests/integration/memory-v2-prod-readiness.test.ts)
7 tests covering full Memory V2 lifecycle:
1. DB initialize + 7 entry types insert (adr, memory, sprint, debt, pattern, retro, identity)
2. Tag many-to-many association (getTagsForEntry, getByTags)
3. Relations (references, supersedes) + getRelations/getRelationsFrom/getRelationsTo
4. FTS5 dual-layer query (TR "kararlı düzgün" + EN "stable safe" + DE "Sicherheit")
5. Decay trigger (sprint 100, decay_after_sprints 3 → old entries "decayed")
6. Export to .md + parse back to DB → roundtrip integrity
7. Combined flow: all operations in one lifecycle

### Test 2: 1000-Entry Stress (tests/integration/memory-v2-stress.test.ts)
8 tests covering performance and scale:
1. 1000 random entry insert (mixed types) — timing
2. 100 random tag associations — verify getByTags
3. 200 random relation inserts — verify countRelations
4. FTS5 search 50 queries (random text) → all < 100ms per query
5. Concurrent read 20 threads (Promise.all 20x query) → no error
6. DB file size report (< 5MB target)
7. Export full DB → .md (< 500ms target)
8. Decay 500 entries → ms measurement

### Approach
- Use temp directories (mkdtempSync) per test suite, cleaned in afterEach
- Follow existing memory-v2.test.ts patterns for imports and setup
- No external dependencies — pure vitest + node:fs + node:os
- Performance measurements via Date.now() deltas
- Deterministic random via simple seed math (no crypto)

### Files to Create
- tests/integration/memory-v2-prod-readiness.test.ts (NEW)
- tests/integration/memory-v2-stress.test.ts (NEW)

